      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\tan x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186176049/tangent.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function $y=\\tan x$ has period $\\pi .$ So, $\\tan (x+\\pi )=\\tan (x)=\\tan (x+2n\\pi )$ for any integer $n.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function $y=\\tan x$ has asymptotes at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function $y=\\tan x$ has period $\\pi .$ So, $\\tan (x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\tan (x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\pi )=\\tan (x+\\frac{3\\pi }{4}).$"
    },
